# Java 21 & Spring Boot 3 Standards

## Language Features

Use modern Java 21 features:

```java
// ✅ Records for DTOs and Value Objects
public record PipelineId(UUID value) {
    public static PipelineId generate() { return new PipelineId(UUID.randomUUID()); }
}

// ✅ Sealed interfaces for domain events
public sealed interface PipelineEvent permits Created, Updated, Published {}

// ✅ Pattern matching in switch
return switch (event) {
    case Created c -> handleCreated(c);
    case Updated u -> handleUpdated(u);
    case Published p -> handlePublished(p);
};

// ✅ Text blocks for SQL/JSON
String sql = """
    SELECT * FROM pipelines
    WHERE tenant_id = :tenantId
    AND status = 'ACTIVE'
    """;
```

## Spring Boot Conventions

```java
// ✅ Constructor injection (no @Autowired on fields)
@Service
public class PipelineService {
    private final PipelineRepository repository;
    private final EventPublisher publisher;
    
    public PipelineService(PipelineRepository repository, EventPublisher publisher) {
        this.repository = repository;
        this.publisher = publisher;
    }
}

// ✅ Use @Transactional at service layer, not repository
@Transactional
public Pipeline createPipeline(CreatePipelineCommand cmd) { ... }

// ✅ Validate inputs with Bean Validation
public record CreatePipelineRequest(
    @NotBlank String name,
    @NotNull @Valid PipelineDefinition definition
) {}
```

## Error Handling

```java
// ✅ Domain-specific exceptions
public class PipelineNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    private final PipelineId pipelineId;
    
    public PipelineNotFoundException(PipelineId id) {
        super("Pipeline not found: " + id);
        this.pipelineId = id;
    }
}

// ✅ Global exception handler
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    @ExceptionHandler(PipelineNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail> handleNotFound(PipelineNotFoundException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(404)
            .body(ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, ex.getMessage()));
    }
}

// ❌ NEVER do this
catch (Exception e) { }  // Silent swallow
catch (Exception e) { e.printStackTrace(); }  // No structured logging
```

## Logging

```java
// ✅ Use SLF4J with structured logging
private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(PipelineService.class);

log.info("Pipeline created", kv("pipelineId", id), kv("tenantId", tenantId));
log.error("Failed to create pipeline", kv("request", request), kv("error", e.getMessage()), e);

// ❌ Never use System.out or string concatenation in logs
System.out.println("Created: " + id);  // Wrong
log.info("Created: " + id);  // Wrong - use structured logging
```
